> them up through R, Rdbi will work, but RdbiPgSQL isn't in the library.  
> 
> Using install.packages2("RdbiPgSQL") gets the same response: it can't find the
> package.
> 

It is only available as a source package, which needs to be built from 
source locally, linked against the local versions of the PostgreSQL 
libraries. I think Markus is not using Windows.

> I also tried to install RMySQL, which is supposed to be supported for R on
> Windows, but isn't in the CRAN repository.
> 

Correct, but visit CRAN, for example:

http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/contrib/2.0/

and read the ReadMe:

"...
Although the packages
  RMySQL, ROracle, and snow
pass make check, it seems to be dangerous to distribute them:
I do not have the software available these packages depend on.
RMySQL is available at http://stat.bell-labs.com/RS-DBI/download,
provided by its maintainer, David A. James."

It's the same thing, you can't automate the building of package binaries 
that depend on possibly varying external headers and libraries.

Roger


